{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfpm9Aa7yK2AYY65ZrTRu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Use the `--repeats` flag. It runs every test the number of times you give it, whether the test passes or fails, so a test that fails on only some runs is likely flaky:\n\n```sh\nnpx vitest run --repeats 10\n```\n\nYou can add a file or name filter to repeat just the tests you suspect, for example `npx vitest run src/foo.test.ts --repeats 20` or `-t \"my test name\"`. Don't use `--retry.count` for this: it only re-runs tests that fail, which hides flakiness instead of exposing it. To repeat a single test without the CLI flag, you can set `{ repeats: 10 }` in that test's options.\n\nSource: [Vitest CLI docs](https://vitest.dev/guide/cli)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":538,"cache_read_input_tokens":4148,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":538},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cb2e846b-7ef4-4633-8e0e-bb4925b8fe4f","uuid":"1d898fdc-205d-40b8-8a54-627eca968077","timestamp":"2026-10-08T12:22:20.600Z","request_id":"req_011Cfpm9AFmj6JF8kBygxnkU"}
